  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe live MCP app accepts `--mcp-idle-timeout <seconds>` and\n`CAMCRAFT_MCP_IDLE_TIMEOUT`. The option wins over the environment value.\nThe default stays 300 seconds. Zero disables idle expiry.\n\nThe app uses the configured window for its TCP listener and authenticated\nUI link clients. The UI link still requires a valid hello within five\nseconds. Framing limits, shutdown polling and one-client ownership stay\nunchanged. The stdio bridge does not reconnect automatically.\n\nInvalid values produce a named startup error. Seconds must be non-negative\nwhole numbers that fit `u64`. The help text, start guide and MCP skill\ndescribe the option.\n\n## Verification\n\nBehavioral red tests on current main proved that zero was clamped to the\npoll step and that the UI rejected the new option. Both now pass.\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_live -- --test-threads=3`\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib cli_options_tests -- --test-threads=3`\n- Selected quick gate (pass: `mcp_live` 29 tests; UI library 1714 passed, 8 ignored): `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --only 'app suites: mcp_live' --only 'ui suites: lib'`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --test mcp_live -- -D warnings`: pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --lib -- -D warnings`: pass.\n- Site tests `test_ai_guide.py` and `test_guide_after_1995.py`: 10 pass.\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\n\nThe tests cover defaults, CLI and environment precedence, zero, invalid and\noverflow values, finite expiry, prompt shutdown and the pre-hello deadline.\nAll socket tests use synthetic local connections.\n\nThe full quick plan selects 179 steps because the MCP re-export maps to\n167 app suites. Only the transport and UI-library steps run here.\n`cargo xtask gate light --dry-run` requires a release build of app and\nmotion plus unrelated geometry tests. The light lane was not run. A dry run\nis not a pass. No post, toolpath, geometry or simulation code changes.\nNo catalog, full-workspace, release, physical-machine or Windows check ran.\n\n## Before and after CLI help\n\nBoth images show actual `target/debug/camcraft-ui --help` output. Each command exited with code 0.\nI built each unmodified revision on Linux with `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo build -j 3 -p camcraft-ui --bin camcraft-ui`.\nThe browser displays the captured stderr. Only ANSI color codes were removed. No help text was edited.\n\n**Before:** parent revision `e6849c5aea183b81135c8143955cc8c88a429a89`.\n\n![Before: executed CLI help without the idle timeout option](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/d0d8be407e8ab9c6d5f4aff85fb32dec627ea3c8/pr4190/before-help.png)\n\n**After:** PR head `5b8c998a4fa96b211be5c27aafe47d1439308381`.\nThe help adds `--mcp-idle-timeout`, `CAMCRAFT_MCP_IDLE_TIMEOUT`, the 300-second default, and the zero-value behavior.\n\n![After: executed CLI help with the idle timeout option](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/d0d8be407e8ab9c6d5f4aff85fb32dec627ea3c8/pr4190/after-help.png)\n\nThe images are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch at `d0d8be407e8ab9c6d5f4aff85fb32dec627ea3c8`.\nNo source commit changed. The [collaborator review](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/4190#issuecomment-7197915002) reports full quick, light, and strict clippy passes on this head.\nThis evidence update does not rerun those gates.\n\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: Configure the live MCP idle window with `--mcp-idle-timeout` or `CAMCRAFT_MCP_IDLE_TIMEOUT`; zero disables idle expiry.\n\nFixes #3940\n",
